Comment: Sparky Stereo OS, Daniel Ramos's (Capitain Jack) edition of SparkyLinux
 (https://sparkylinux.org, by Paweł "pavroo" Pijanowski).
 .
 The module is built against OBS Studio's libobs and obs-frontend-api (original
 author Lain Bailey, with the contributors in OBS's AUTHORS file, GPL-2.0-or-later,
 https://obsproject.com) as deb-multimedia packages them (Christian Marillat).
 Its encoder paths, muxer helper, plugin loader and frontend were read in OBS
 Studio 33.0.1; the filter's render follows the pattern of OBS's own crop filter.
 No code is copied from OBS. The packing list and the video layout rule come from
 the stereo layer (libstereo-policy, LGPL-2.1-or-later) and its translations from
 the layer's catalogue; the unpacking rule and the anaglyph table follow the
 layer's storedView() and Picture::anaglyphTransform(). x264 (VideoLAN and the
 x264 authors) writes the frame packing arrangement message through its own
 frame-packing option.

